---
import { btnCls, cardCls, crumbCls, emptyCls, fieldCls, rangeCls, selectCls, tabCls, tabsCls } from '../lib/ui';
// One size (a model size): the template every size on the ladder uses (UI.md, "Model pages"). It lives at
// #/classes/<class>[/overview|/training|/scoring|/waypoints] and has five tabs of its own:
//   Fleet     the ships of this size (the default)
//   Overview  the model's performance in as few charts as possible
//   Training  what it was trained on and how: the model, every run's setup, loss, the shelves
//   Scoring   every score on its runs, in two parts: science (how well it predicts text it has
//             never seen) and art (how its writing compares with real books)
//   Waypoints the moments it passes in training: Nevermores (induction heads) forming, traits emerging
// A panel that belongs to one kind of model only carries data-kind (the proxy's calibration).
---
<div class="section" id="rung">
  <h1><a class={crumbCls('back')} href="/harbours">← harbours</a> <span id="rungtitle"></span> <span class="q" id="rungjob"></span></h1>
  <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="modelnav">
    <a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="overview">Overview</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="goals">Goals</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="training">Training</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="scoring">Scoring</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="waypoints">Waypoints</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="fitouts">Fitouts</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-mtab="bet">Bet</a>
  </nav>

  <!-- ============================== Fleet: the ships of this size -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="goals">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="goalsover"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Filling the seven steps <span class="note">the goal: as many tricks as this ship can learn, building on everything below it, so the route fills as fast as it can. Green is performed by this size, outlined is inherited from a smaller size (carried up, still to show here), grey is open</span></h2>
      <div class="coverage" id="goalcoverage"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>What the field expects of this size <span class="note">the minimum, not the limit: the tricks the field would expect a ship this size to reach, and how its voyages are doing on each; every trick above them is worth taking too. Sort by any column, filter by step</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools" data-filters><label class="note" for="goalfilter">step to quantum physics</label><select class={selectCls('')} id="goalfilter" data-remember title="filter the goals by waypoint"><option value="">all seven</option></select></div>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="goaltable" class="clickable"><thead><tr><th>trick</th><th>waypoint</th><th>gate</th><th>rests on</th><th>the field shows it at</th><th>on this size</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Overview -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="overview">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="sopsummarypanel">
      <h2>The SOP run, and what it means <span class="note">this ship's newest voyage: the standard it was built to, its scores, and what those numbers say about that standard — a reading, not a verdict on the ship alone</span></h2>
      <div id="sopsummary"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the voyage…</div></div>
    </section>
    
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="gridpanel">
      <h2>Every voyage at this size <span class="note">one square per voyage in the order they started; the brighter the green, the better (lower) its Forgotten Tomes bits per byte, by quartile of the voyages scored so far; an outlined square is running</span></h2>
      <div id="rungridsum" class="gridsum"></div>
      <div id="rungrid"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The Forgotten Tomes score, voyage by voyage <span class="note">bits per byte on 16 books Qwen 3.8 cannot have read, lower is better; one dot per scored voyage in the order they started, the line is the best so far, dotted lines are Qwen models scored the same way</span></h2>
      <div class="chart tall" id="ftchart"></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Training -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="training">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The star chart, against Qwen3 4B <span class="note">the ten points of the chart, each reading divided by its own mark: Qwen3 4B (which chains) against this ship's newest voyage, read live while it trains. Above the dotted line a point clears its mark; the gap between the lines is how far the ship is behind on that point, and where its line is above, it is ahead</span></h2>
      <div class="chart" id="sizejourney"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <div class="handtools" style="border:0;padding:0;margin:0"><label class="note" for="soppick">SOP version</label><select class={selectCls('')} id="soppick" data-remember></select><span class="note" id="sopnote">every run, chart and reading below is built to this version (or to all of them)</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="watchpanel">
      <h2>Watch it train <span class="note">this size's voyage at sea (else its latest home), read every 30 seconds: where it is in its stages and passes, the cards it has drawn and when, and the readings that matter, by tokens read</span></h2>
      <div id="watchhead" class="watchhead"><div class={emptyCls()}>looking for a voyage…</div></div>
      <div id="watchstages" class="watchstages"></div>
      <div id="watchdrawn" class="watchdrawn"></div>
      <div class="watchgrid">
        <div><h3>Loss and learning rate</h3><div class="chart" id="watchloss"></div></div>
        <div><h3>Judge books, bits per byte <span class="s">lower is better</span></h3><div class="chart" id="watchbpb"></div></div>
        <div><h3>Shapes <span class="s">top guess right</span></h3><div class="chart" id="watchshapes"></div></div>
        <div><h3>The cards <span class="s">each against its mark</span></h3><div class="chart" id="watchcards"></div></div>
        <div><h3>Copying and chaining <span class="s">copy gain (nats), one-hop lift, cause gain</span></h3><div class="chart" id="watchchain"></div></div>
        <div><h3>The log</h3><pre id="watchlog" class="watchlog"></pre></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="rungover" id="rungover"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Training loss <span class="note">nats per token on the training library, the latest 12 voyages at this size</span></h2>
      <div class="chart" id="losschart"></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Scoring -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="scoring">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="cardstrippanel">
      <h2>The four cards <span class="note">what a model must hold before it can chain (every model that chains holds all four): each card's best reading by a voyage of this size against its mark, held when a voyage ended lit, touched when one only passed it; beside them, whether it chains cause and effect</span></h2>
      <div id="cardstrip" class="cardstrip"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the cards…</div></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>On the route to quantum physics <span class="note">the seven waypoints, bottom to top; the tricks the field expects of this size are lit, those it carries up from smaller sizes are marked, and those the field expects only of bigger sizes are faded: still worth taking. ◆ is a gate: performed before a ship moves on to the next waypoint. Open a trick for its stars and progress</span></h2>
      <div class="goalroute" id="goalroute"></div>
    </section>

    <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="scnav"><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="maths">Maths</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="ask">Ask</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="language">Language</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="shapes">Shapes</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="number">Number</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="physics">Physics</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="life">Life</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="return">Return</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="logic">Logic</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-ssub="versus">Versus</a></nav>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="ask">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="askpanel">
      <h2>Ask the best version <span class="note">type a line and read what it guesses comes next: its ten likeliest next words (or two words, or the raw pieces it actually predicts), no sampling; or let it answer; the rudimentary questions below each carry the answer we would hope for, and "run all" shows where that answer ranks among its guesses</span></h2>
      <div id="askwho" class="askwho"></div>
      <div class="askrow">
        <select class={selectCls()} id="askvoyage" aria-label="the voyage to ask"></select>
        <select class={selectCls()} id="askmode" aria-label="what to guess">
          <option value="1">guess the next word</option><option value="2">guess the next two words</option><option value="pieces">guess the next piece (as it sees it)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <textarea class={fieldCls()} id="asktext" rows="2" placeholder="Once upon a"></textarea>
      <div class="askrow">
        <button class={btnCls('default')} id="askguess" type="button">Guess</button>
        <button class={btnCls()} id="askanswer" type="button">Answer</button>
        <button class={btnCls()} id="askall" type="button">Run all the questions</button>
      </div>
      <div id="askchips" class="askchips"></div>
      <div id="askout" class="askout"></div>
    </section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="maths">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="mathspanel">
      <h2>The maths book <span class="note">nine chapters after Augustus De Morgan's <i>Elements of Arithmetic</i>, his sections in his order, eight sums each in plain words ("Two and three make"); each chapter opens its section of the book in the reader; each sum's answer against its rival, the answer of the mistake a learner makes at that chapter. A sum is right when the answer is among the ship's ten guesses and above the rival; a chapter is learnt at six of eight; the ship has learnt the book up to the first chapter it has not</span></h2>
      <div class="askrow">
        <select class={selectCls()} id="mathssop" aria-label="the SOP version to read the book from" title="the SOP version: only voyages built to it are offered"></select>
        <select class={selectCls()} id="mathsvoyage" aria-label="the voyage to read the book with"></select>
        <button class={btnCls('default')} id="mathsrun" type="button">Read the book</button>
      </div>
      <div id="mathsout" class="askout"></div>
    </section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="language">
    <h2 class="band">Science <span class="q">how well it predicts text it has never seen: bits per byte, lower is better</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>What we measure <span class="note">"to come" is not built yet</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="sciencemetrics"><thead><tr><th>metric</th><th>what it tells us</th><th>better is</th><th>state</th><th id="scorenowhead">now</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Scoreboard <span class="note">the Forgotten Tomes and the voyage's English held-out books, then the held-out score by kind of byte <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="scienceboard"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="calpanel" data-kind="proxy" hidden>
      <h2>Calibration against 9m <span class="note">the same library and passes at both sizes; the proxy is trusted only if it orders the libraries as 9m does. Forgotten Tomes bits per byte, English, lower is better</span></h2>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="scroll"><table id="caltable"><thead><tr><th>library</th><th>passes</th><th>9m voyage</th><th>9m score</th><th>1m voyage</th><th>1m score</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
          <p class="note" id="calverdict"></p></div>
        <div class="chart" id="calchart"></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Bits per byte by kind of byte <span class="note">spelling is "inside a word"; one bar per voyage; lower is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="splitchart"></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The Forgotten Tomes, book by book <span class="note">the best voyage at this size, the latest voyages and Qwen; click a book to read it</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll bookswrap"><table id="tomestable" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>

    <h2 class="band">Art <span class="q">how its writing compares with real books: the laws of text, grammar, voice</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>What we measure <span class="note">"to come" is not built yet</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="artmetrics"><thead><tr><th>metric</th><th>what it tells us</th><th>better is</th><th>state</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Scoreboard <span class="note">the laws on the text it writes, model beside the books' own value (ref) <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="artboard"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The laws: model against the books <span class="note">model value ÷ the books' value; closer to the dotted line at 1 is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="lawchart"></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="shapes">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Shapes <span class="note">the parts-of-speech taxonomy at every reading (s5_policy/taxonomy.py): is the top guess the right part of speech, the right Ogden kind (thing, quality, operation, mark), the right keyed word; and what kind of word it expects against what the judge books hold</span></h2>
        <div class="chart" id="shapeschart"></div>
        <div id="shapesmass" class="shapesmass"></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="number">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2 id="subj-number-title">Number <span class="note" id="subj-number-about"></span></h2>
        <div id="subj-number" class="subject"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the tests…</div></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="physics">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2 id="subj-physics-title">Physics <span class="note" id="subj-physics-about"></span></h2>
        <div id="subj-physics" class="subject"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the tests…</div></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="life">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2 id="subj-life-title">Life <span class="note" id="subj-life-about"></span></h2>
        <div id="subj-life" class="subject"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the tests…</div></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="return">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2 id="subj-return-title">Return <span class="note" id="subj-return-about"></span></h2>
        <div id="subj-return" class="subject"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the tests…</div></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="versus">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Versus <span class="note">this size's voyage against a reference model on every reading both have: the trick tests, the logic deck, the cards and copying, and the judge books' bits per byte; each put as a share of the reference's level so they rank together</span></h2>
        <div id="vspick" class="vspick"></div>
        <div id="vsbody"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading…</div></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="ssub" data-ssub="logic">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2 id="subj-logic-title">Logic <span class="note" id="subj-logic-about"></span></h2>
        <div id="subj-logic" class="subject"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the tests…</div></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================== Waypoints -->
  <!-- ============================== Bet: the Navigator's Wager (thorp/viable/s4_intelligence/wager.py) -->
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="bet">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="wagerpanel">
      <h2>The Navigator's Wager <span class="note">pull one lever on a voyage and bet where the 16 cards fall: for each card, does the pull make it appear, vanish, come earlier or later, or stay the same (and, for a bonus, in which layer)? The House bets that nothing moves. Five chips a round; the readings reveal it; ties go to the House. What a round reveals is the lever's lesson</span></h2>
      <div class="wagerdeal">
        <label>Control voyage <select class={selectCls()} id="wagercontrol"></select></label>
        <label>Lever <select class={selectCls()} id="wagerlever"></select></label>
        <button class={btnCls('default')} id="wagerdealbtn" type="button">Deal the round</button>
        <span class="s" id="wagerleverabout"></span>
      </div>
      <div id="wagerrounds" class="wagerrounds"></div>
      <div id="wagerhead" class="wagerhead"></div>
      <div id="wagertable" class="wagertable"></div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="fitouts">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Fitouts <span class="note">the training material curated for this size, matched to its stages: pretraining (in order, one voyage) and post-training (in order, each seeded from the one before); then the four necessary cards each stage has drawn so far, voyage by voyage</span></h2>
      <div id="classfitouts"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the fitouts…</div></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="mtab" data-mtab="waypoints">
    <!-- the three steps a size proves in order: match the field, beat it at this size, then reach up -->
    <nav class={tabsCls('line', 'subnav')} data-orientation="horizontal" data-variant="line" id="wpnav"><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="expected">1 · Expected</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="envelope">2 · Pushing the envelope</a><a class={tabCls('')} data-state="inactive" data-wsub="stars">3 · Exploring the stars</a></nav>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><div class="wpsteps" id="wpsteps"></div>
      <div class="handtools mt" data-filters><label class="note" for="wpfilter">step to quantum physics</label><select class={selectCls('')} id="wpfilter" data-remember title="filter the tricks by waypoint"><option value="">all seven</option></select></div></section>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="expected">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Expected <span class="note">what the field already shows at this size or smaller: the tricks to prove first, so the ship is known to match the field before it tries to beat it</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-expected" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="envelope">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Pushing the envelope <span class="note">this size's goals, and those it carries up from smaller sizes, that nobody has shown at this size: the field shows them only in bigger models</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-envelope" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>
    <div class="wsub" data-wsub="stars">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Exploring the stars <span class="note">the ambitious tricks: goals of the bigger sizes, nearest first. A ship of this size performing one is a find</span></h2>
        <div class="scroll"><table id="wp-stars" class="clickable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
    </div>

    <h2 class="band">The instruments <span class="q">the stars, Nevermores and traits as measured on this size's voyages, behind the tricks above</span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Stars in reach <span class="note">the kinds of head this size is expected to reach (the star chart's "expected from" at or below it), and how its own voyages are doing on each; <span id="reachnext"></span></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="reachtable"><thead><tr><th>kind of head</th><th>family</th><th>expected from</th><th>why</th><th>on this size</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Waypoints, voyage by voyage <span class="note">the training step at which each voyage first passed each waypoint; "not yet" is measured but not reached, – is not measured on that voyage <b class="recentnote"></b></span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="waypointtable"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <h2 class="band">Nevermores <span class="q">induction heads: at a word seen before, a head looks back to what followed it last time and bets it comes again; they form suddenly</span><span class="bandtools"><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} data-essay="nevermore">Read: what a Nevermore is</button><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} id="readpassage">Read the test passage</button></span></h2>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')} id="handpanel">
      <h2>The hand <span class="note">each card is one attention head, rows by layer from the top; a card turns face up (♠) when its head becomes a Nevermore, 0.3 or more on either test; until then its face shows through as far as the head has come. The big number is the real-prose score, the corner one the random test. Bigger models show their strongest five</span></h2>
      <div class="handtools"><select class={selectCls('')} id="handrun" title="the voyage whose hand is shown"></select>
        <button class={btnCls('outline', '')} id="handplay" title="deal the hand step by step">▶ play</button>
        <input class={rangeCls('')} type="range" id="handstep" min="0" max="0" value="0"><span id="handlabel"></span></div>
      <div id="hand"></div>
    </section>
    <div class="row">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>The strongest head <span class="note">its Nevermore score on a real passage read twice, by training step (where one shows first); the line crossing 0.3 is the moment a Nevermore forms; the latest 12 voyages</span></h2><div class="chart" id="nvchart"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Copy gain <span class="note">nats per token the model saves on the second copy of a sequence, which only a model that copies can; higher is better</span></h2><div class="chart" id="copychart"></div></section>
    </div>
    <h2 class="band">Traits <span class="q">can its hidden state tell fiction, verse and first person apart on books it has never read; found at the dotted line, learned when it also clears the bag-of-tokens and untrained-model floors</span><span class="bandtools"><button class={btnCls('outline', '')} data-essay="traits">Read: how traits are found</button></span></h2>
    <div class="row3">
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Fiction</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-fiction"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>Verse</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-verse"></div></section>
      <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}><h2>First person</h2><div class="chart short" id="trait-first_person"></div></section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
